      "created_at": "2015-04-22T16:03:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Just thought it was worth reporting. &nbsp;My buddy and I were playing a game the other night, and I played Rogue Agent Knyfe. &nbsp;We started talking about various combos while we played. &nbsp;After the game was over, we decided to try out a comp that worked really well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SS Tachyon, Rogue Agent KNYFE, O-X, and Kvothe AA.</p><p>The idea is, everyone just uses their powers to play Tachyon's deck. &nbsp;Additionally, AA can use Vernal Sonata to put back Lightspeed Barrages that might end up getitng played at inopportune times. &nbsp;It worked about as well as expected (VERY WELL). &nbsp;We couldn't decide whether to call the comp \"World's Fastest Tachyon\" or \"Everyone plays Tachyon's Deck\". &nbsp;Regardless, it went VERY well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, does anybody else out there have some particularly fun/broken comps?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:36.059Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
