      "raw": "<p>Just thought it was worth reporting. &nbsp;My buddy and I were playing a game the other night, and I played Rogue Agent Knyfe. &nbsp;We started talking about various combos while we played. &nbsp;After the game was over, we decided to try out a comp that worked really well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SS Tachyon, Rogue Agent KNYFE, O-X, and Kvothe AA.</p><p>The idea is, everyone just uses their powers to play Tachyon&#39;s deck. &nbsp;Additionally, AA can use Vernal Sonata to put back Lightspeed Barrages that might end up getitng played at inopportune times. &nbsp;It worked about as well as expected (VERY WELL). &nbsp;We couldn&#39;t decide whether to call the comp &quot;World&#39;s Fastest Tachyon&quot; or &quot;Everyone plays Tachyon&#39;s Deck&quot;. &nbsp;Regardless, it went VERY well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, does anybody else out there have some particularly fun/broken comps?</p>",
